# claude-mv — per-machine config
#
# Copy this file to `.env` beside claude-mv.zsh and adjust. The .env is
# gitignored.
#
# Sourcing convention: claude-mv sources this file *inside* its own function
# scope and declares every key `local` first, so `typeset` (without -g) keeps
# the values function-local — nothing leaks into the interactive shell.

# Claude Code profile dirs whose history claude-mv migrates on a move.
#
# Leave this unset unless the detection is wrong for this machine. Unset,
# claude-mv asks the companion `claude-profile` juggler when it is installed —
# that tool is the registry of config dirs, so a profile added there is
# migrated here with no second edit — and otherwise falls back to ~/.claude
# plus ~/.claude-personal when it exists.
#
# Setting it pins the list and skips both. Note that means a profile
# claude-profile knows about but this list omits is NOT migrated: its history
# stays keyed on the old path, silently.
#typeset -a CLAUDE_PROFILE_DIRS=("$HOME/.claude" "$HOME/.claude-personal")

# Keep the restore point after a successful overwrite, as the archive of the
# discarded destination history. Default: 1 (kept). Set 0 to opt out —
# overwrite then cleans up its restore point like the other modes do.
#typeset CLAUDE_MV_OVERWRITE_BACKUP=1

# Where restore points live. Default: ~/.claude-mv/restore
#typeset CLAUDE_MV_RESTORE_ROOT="$HOME/.claude-mv/restore"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --extract (moving individual sessions rather than a folder) has two soft
# dependencies. Neither is required: without them the sessions are listed
# straight off disk and chosen from a numbered prompt. These are env vars
# rather than .env keys — they exist to pin a path for a one-off run or a
# test, not to configure a machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# CLAUDE_MV_CCFIND_SCRIPT   where ccfind.zsh lives, when it is neither loaded
#                           as a function nor a sibling clone next to this
#                           repo. Authoritative like CLAUDE_PROFILE_SCRIPT: if
#                           it points nowhere, ccfind counts as not installed.
#
# CLAUDE_MV_SOURCE          ccfind | fs | auto (default auto). Which source
#                           lists the sessions. `ccfind` fails loudly rather
#                           than falling back, which is what you want when
#                           you meant to use it.
#
# CLAUDE_MV_PICKER          fzf | plain | auto (default auto). `plain` is the
#                           numbered prompt, and the one a pipe can drive.
